<h1>Preferences - Datums - Sheet Metal</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p>Sheet Metal settings define behaviour of the software when capture of circular hole with some thickness.</p>
<p><img src="Images/preferences_datums_sheet_metal.gif" width="593px" height="367px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
<p class="sub-head">Sheet metal measurement group</p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;">Measuring sheet metal circles is similar to ordinary circle capture except for probe compensation. If the equator of the ball probe is not in the range of material thickness, a different radius is used for probe compensation. This is dependent on the depth of penetration of the ball probe, relative to the base plane of the circle. There are three cases:</p>
<ol>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps">When probe equator is within the Thickness zone the compensation is with the probe radius.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps">When probe equator is in Zone A or Zone B (the thickness of the two zones is equal to the probe radius) the compensation ranges from 0 to the probe radius depending on the depth of the probe centre.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps">When probe equator is outside Zone A, Thickness zone, and Zone B the point is discarded and optionally a warning sound is played.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><img src="Images/material_thickness.gif" width="532px" height="199px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Sheet metal measurement</b></span> checkbox</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>T</b></span>his option enables and disables sheet metal measurement functionality. It is disabled by default.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Thickness</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">The amount of material thickness. Default value is 0.7mm.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Enable sound warning</b></span> checkbox</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">When this option is enabled a warning sound is played when the captured point is outside Zone A, Thickness zone, and Zone B. It is enabled by default.</p>
